5. **Test `ids_hold_across_a_fresh_process`, and its child.**
   - The parent computes the id strings of `stand::boot` for each lean task in both modes. The timer goes through `boot_timer` with no ticks delivered.
   - It then runs `std::process::Command::new(std::env::current_exe()…)` with `["--ignored", "--exact", "ids_in_a_child_process", "--nocapture"]`, the precedent form at `telemetry_stdout_silent.rs:10-11`.
   - The child, `#[test] #[ignore = "spawned as a child process by ids_hold_across_a_fresh_process"]`, prints one line `pid {std::process::id()}`. Then, for each task and mode, it prints one line per id, each prefixed with a fixed marker that the parent filters on.
   - The parent asserts:
     - the child exited successfully;
     - the child's pid differs from `std::process::id()`;
     - the child's id list is non-empty for every task and mode;
     - the child's list equals the parent's, in order.
   - The ids travel only over the child's captured stdout into the parent's assertion. They are never logged and never committed (per obs-plan §8; security-plan §Logging & Monitoring).

- **Coverage of new surfaces:**
  - `stand_id_persistence` child re-exec (test-only process spawn) → validation {n/a — fixed argv, no input} · instrumentation {n/a — test code; census gate `last line 0`} · PII {n/a — ids travel only over captured stdout into an assertion, never logged} · tests {integration 3} · a11y n/a · tokens n/a
  - CRUD row key / `Person.id` (model change, no new UI element) → validation {n/a — the id is a model-assigned `u64`} · instrumentation n/a · PII n/a · tests {stand_id_persistence; stand_crud 2, stand_element_ids 4 green unchanged} · a11y {roles, focusability and Tab order untouched — `ci-leg.sh a11y` green; after a remount, focus is never on a dropped node} · tokens {n/a — class/style/CSS unchanged, entry 3 `presentation-unchanged`}

3. **Grammar unit tests** — seven new tests in `element_id.rs`'s `mod tests`, each an app as a plain
   `fn() -> Element`:
   - `a_keyed_parent_anchors_its_unkeyed_children` — children and a grandchild of `div#box` read `box//span:0`,
     `box//p:0`, `box//p:0/b:0`;
   - `the_nearest_keyed_ancestor_anchors` — under `div#outer { div#inner { i {} } u {} }` the `i` reads
     `inner//i:0` and the `u` reads `outer//u:0`;
   - `an_unusable_id_anchors_nothing` — children of an element whose `id` is empty, holds a `/`, or repeats an
     earlier one read plain paths with no `//`;
   - `a_component_root_under_a_keyed_element_restarts_at_its_chain` — `div#slot { Item {} }` leaves Item's
     root at `Item/b:0`;
   - `a_key_spelled_like_a_component_stays_distinct` — a `div` with `id: "Item"` holding a `b`, beside an
     `Item {}` component whose root is a `b`, reads `Item//b:0` and `Item/b:0`, and the whole list is distinct;
   - `a_dioxus_keyed_row_under_a_keyed_list_reads_its_key_segment` — `ul#list` with keyed `li` rows reads
     `list//li[ada]`, `list//li[grace]`;
   - `an_edit_outside_the_anchor_keeps_the_anchored_id` — two apps, the second with an earlier same-tag sibling
     and a wrapper outside `#box`: the anchored ids are equal; a third with an earlier same-tag sibling inside
     `#box`: the anchored id differs.
   The six existing tests keep their pins: none has an unkeyed child under a keyed same-owner parent (sweep,
   research.md §Files inspected), and the skeleton's `main` anchors nothing because its children are another
   owner's roots.

5. **Library unit tests** — four tests in `actionable.rs`'s `mod tests`:
   - `an_unkeyed_actionable_element_is_reported_with_its_remedy` — a fixture with an unkeyed button, an unkeyed
     disabled button, an unkeyed `div` with a click handler, a button whose `id` repeats an earlier one, and a
     keyed button: exactly the first four are returned, each naming the reader that matched;
   - `a_keyed_or_inert_element_is_not_reported` — keyed controls and plain `div`, `p` and `label` elements
     return nothing;
   - `a_hidden_or_disabled_control_is_still_held` — a `display: none` button with a handler and a disabled
     input, both unkeyed, are returned;
   - `the_report_names_structure_never_content` — `remedy()` and the entry's fields hold the id, tag and role
     and none of the fixture's text, names or attribute values.

- **The edits that must keep an id.** Verified in shape against `element_id.rs` (research.md §Patterns detected):
  - an element that reads its **author key** keeps its id under every edit that leaves it in place: handler, state, text, attribute and style changes; siblings added or removed anywhere, an earlier same-tag sibling included; an ancestor wrapped or unwrapped. True today already — the key replaces the path (element_id.rs:170-176);
  - an **unkeyed** element keeps its id under every edit outside the subtree of the ancestor its path starts at, and under edits inside that subtree that do not touch its own relative path (later siblings, other-tag siblings, behaviour and content changes);
  - `[premise-corrected: the "no keyed ancestor" case is nearly empty — the document skeleton's mount element reads the author key main and is an ancestor of every vdom-rendered element (dioxus_document.rs:126-131; measured id list, research.md), so a literal "nearest keyed ancestor" always exists. Whether main, and a keyed container outside an element's own component, anchor it is the composition fork below]`.

9. **Unit tests** — an inline `#[cfg(test)] mod tests` in snapshot.rs, built like the `element_id` unit tests: a
   `DioxusDocument` from a small plain app (per test-plan §3 · §4). It covers these cases:
   - an `aria-label`ed button reads that label as its name;
   - a `<label for>`-bound input reads the label's text;
   - a text-only `p` reads its text;
   - a `display:none` subtree is absent;
   - a disabled button reads `enabled: Some(false)`;
   - a checkbox reads `checked: Some(…)`;
   - a text input reads its value;
   - text runs are never nodes;
   - every id equals `element_id` of its element.

